Iteration 

Sets are mentioned such as. A set is an object that can be itered in a for loop. Unlike the keys in a dictionary the order of a set will be determined by the hash table underlying the set.
"Hash randomization" with the purpose of preventing malicious DoS on hash tables so everytime you start the interpreter a different hash table will be deployed, meaning different order iteration

Operators 

len(s) - Returns the numbers of all elements contained in set s
x in s - True if x is contained in set s, otherwise False
x not in s - True if x is not contained in set s, otherwise False
s <= t - True if set s is a subset of set t, otherwise False
s < t - True if set s is proper subset of set t, otherwise False
s >= t -True if set t is a subset of set s, otherwise False
s > t - True if set t is a proper subset of set s, otherwise False
s | t - Creates a new set containing all elements of s and t. Forms the union of two sets
s & t - Creates a new set containing the objects that are both elements of set s and elements of set t. Forms intersection of two sets 
s - t - Creates a new set with all elements of s except those also contained in t. Difference of sets
s ^ t - Creates a new set containing all objects that occur in either s or t, but not both

Augmented assignments also exists for some of the operators

s |= t - s = s | t
s &= t - s = s & t
s -= t - s = s - t
s ^= t - s = s ^ t

These operators also exists for frozenset but instead of changing the set, it creates a new frozen set instance 

